---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Robert Potts — Child Literacy" active="volunteering">
  <div class="page volunteering">
    <PageHeader title="Child Literacy" />

    <div class="volunteering__grid">
      <div class="volunteering__body">
        <p>
          My mother, as a child, was saved by books. Born into poverty in Monmouth then raised
          by her divorced mother in South London during the war, she had - for many reasons - no
          stability in her life. But one thing her mother did give her was books. They read
          together even during bombings (her mother disliked the shelters). All through her
          life, my mother remembered being given an edition of the Iliad, allegedly retrieved
          from a bomb site; of the worlds this opened up. (She could still recite, right to the
          end, huge amounts of the literature she read as a child.)
        </p>
        <p>
          My bookish mother gained a scholarship to Christ Hospital School, a charity school,
          where she boarded, and had a schedule, and finally felt safe. (And was given her first
          dressing gown!) And from there received an education that led to an exhibition to St
          Anne's College Oxford where she went on to take a First in Modern Languages. That
          Iliad, snatched from the rubble, changed my mother's life. For many children, books are
          an escape; for some, they are also a ladder.
        </p>
        <p>
          My mother was able to give her own children the stability she had lacked, and a
          privileged education. I know how lucky I was, and am determined to give something
          back, and to ensure that other children have the sort of life-changing experiences
          that my mother did.
        </p>
        <h2 class="volunteering__heading">Governance</h2>
        <p>
          I am a Non-Executive Director and Trustee of Barton Academy Trust (BCAT), a
          multi-academy trust in Kent that oversees three schools and is in the process of
          taking in a fourth. They specialise in turning around schools which are struggling,
          and improving the life chances of children from deprived backgrounds. I sit on the
          Finance Committee and the Audit and Risk Committee, and also attend Quality Assurance
          meetings at the Charles Dickens School in Thanet.
        </p>
        <h2 class="volunteering__heading">Volunteering</h2>
        <p>
          I also volunteer, through the charity Schoolreaders, as a reading assistant at a
          primary school in Dover with a high proportion of SEND children. I sit with the
          children as they read to me, and give them one-to-one encouragement and assistance.
          This has been one of the greatest experiences of my life. To be greeted by a Year 8
          child on my second week with the words "Are you reading with us today, Mr Potts?
          HURRAH!" was unforgettable and uplifting.
        </p>
        <p>
          And this summer I had the pleasure of volunteering with the Canterbury Children's
          Literature Festival, "an annual celebration of stories and literacy, focusing on
          inclusion, accessibility and celebrating the joy of stories in all their forms".
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="volunteering__gallery" aria-label="Photos">
        <figure class="volunteering__photo">
          <img src="/images/volunteering/photo-1.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Bunny and Monkey at Fenwick, Canterbury Children's Literature Festival 2026</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="volunteering__photo">
          <img src="/images/volunteering/photo-2.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Mama G's Storytime, Waterstones, Canterbury Children's Literature Festival 2026</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="volunteering__photo">
          <img src="/images/volunteering/photo-3.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Year 4 end-of-term cards, 2026</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .volunteering {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }
  .volunteering__grid {
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .volunteering__body {
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .volunteering__body a {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .placeholder-note {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .volunteering__heading {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .volunteering__gallery {
    /* Stretches to the full height of the grid row (i.e. matches the prose
       column) so space-between can put the first photo's top and the last
       photo's bottom exactly level with the text, whatever its length. */
    align-self: stretch;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    /* Optical nudge: a text line's cap-height sits below its line-box top,
       so an image's hard top edge otherwise looks a fraction high next to it. */
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  .volunteering__photo {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .volunteering__photo img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .volunteering__photo figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .volunteering__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .volunteering__gallery {
      align-self: auto;
      flex-direction: row;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      justify-content: flex-start;
      gap: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
      margin-top: 0;
    }
    .volunteering__photo {
      flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 0.75rem);
      min-width: 10rem;
    }
  }
</style>
